    <h2>The Route: What to Expect</h2>
    <p>
        The drive follows the national highway west from Chittorgarh through the rolling countryside of Mewar. It is a
        well-maintained four-lane road with dhabas and fuel stations along the way, so the journey is comfortable even for
        families with children and elderly travellers.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Sanwariya Seth Temple:</strong> About 40 km from Chittorgarh, a short detour from the highway. Many travellers stop for darshan &ndash; read our <a href="Sanwariya-Seth-Temple-Taxi-from-Chittorgarh.aspx">Sanwariya Seth guide</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Udaipur Airport (Dabok):</strong> The Maharana Pratap Airport lies right on this route, about 22 km before Udaipur city. See our <a href="Udaipur-Airport-to-Chittorgarh-Taxi.aspx">airport transfer guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Things to Do in Udaipur</h2>
    <p>Once you arrive in the City of Lakes, your driver can take you around the main sights:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>City Palace</strong> &ndash; the grand palace complex overlooking Lake Pichola.</li>
        <li><strong>Lake Pichola boat ride</strong> &ndash; with views of Jag Mandir and the Lake Palace.</li>
        <li><strong>Jagdish Temple</strong> &ndash; a beautiful 17th-century temple near the City Palace.</li>
        <li><strong>Fateh Sagar Lake</strong> and <strong>Saheliyon ki Bari</strong> garden.</li>
        <li><strong>Sajjangarh (Monsoon Palace)</strong> &ndash; best at sunset.</li>
        <li>Day trips to <strong>Nathdwara</strong>, <strong>Eklingji</strong>, <strong>Haldighati</strong> and <strong>Kumbhalgarh</strong>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why Book a Taxi Instead of Bus or Train?</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Door-to-door:</strong> Pickup from your home or hotel in Chittorgarh and drop at your hotel in Udaipur.</li>
        <li><strong>Flexible timing:</strong> Leave whenever you like, with no waiting for schedules.</li>
        <li><strong>Stops on your terms:</strong> Temple darshan, tea breaks or photo stops whenever you want.</li>
        <li><strong>Great value for groups:</strong> For 4 or more people, a taxi often costs about the same as individual tickets.</li>
        <li><strong>Luggage friendly:</strong> No hauling bags through stations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Tips for a Smooth Trip</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Book a day in advance during the tourist season (October to March) and long weekends.</li>
        <li>If you have a flight, plan to reach Udaipur Airport at least 2 hours before departure.</li>
        <li>Combine the trip with Chittorgarh Fort sightseeing in the morning if you are short on time &ndash; see our <a href="Chittorgarh-Fort-Travel-Guide.aspx">fort guide</a>.</li>
        <li>Ask about our round-trip packages if you want the driver to wait and bring you back the same day.</li>
    </ul>

